# Project One Get-Item Pseudocode
#
# Graded checkpoint: Module Five Project One
# Later use: get-item and inventory design for M7 Project Two
#
# Review the course-provided get-item flowchart before completing this file.
# Write pseudocode, not Python code. Use clear indentation and course-appropriate
# keywords such as INPUT, OUTPUT, IF, ELSE, SET, ADD, or similar terms.

START get_item

    # TODO 1: Identify the information the get-item process needs.
    SET current_room TO player's current location
    SET room_item TO item located in current_room
    SET player_inventory TO player's current collection list

    # TODO 2: Prompt for and receive the player's get-item command.
    OUTPUT "Enter command (example: get [item]): "
    INPUT player_command

    # TODO 3: Validate whether the requested item is available in the current room.
    IF player_command CONTAINS room_item THEN
        
        # TODO 4: Describe what happens when the item request is valid.
        IF room_item IS NOT IN player_inventory THEN
            ADD room_item TO player_inventory
            OUTPUT "You picked up the " + room_item + "!"
        ELSE
            OUTPUT "You already have this item in your inventory."
        ENDIF

    # TODO 5: Describe what happens when the item request is invalid.
    ELSE
        OUTPUT "That item is not in this room!"
    ENDIF

    # TODO 6: Show how the process returns to the larger gameplay loop.
    RETURN to main game loop

END get_item


